  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday Night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1107 AM CDT Wed May 13 2026\n\nWe'll have one more cool night with temperatures starting in the \nlower 40s to lower 50s Friday morning. Temperatures will rebound \nwith southerly low level flow ramping up on Friday. For the weekend, \ntemperatures will increase each day with the NBM showing about a 50-\n70% chance that BNA reaches 90 degrees for the first time in 2026. \nThere is a low chance of a shower or storm on Saturday with a weak \nwave moving across zonal upper flow, otherwise it will feel like an \nearly summer weekend. The warm pattern will continue into early next \nweek before rain chances increase during the mid week period as a \nlarge upper trough shifts from the Pacific Northwest towards the \nmiddle of the country.",
